**Part 1: Analysis and Description of the Attached PDF**

The attached PDF presents two related research articles investigating Nano-11, a dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle derived from sweet corn, as a vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11 (70-80 nm, positive surface charge) efficiently adsorbs protein antigens and is readily taken up by dendritic cells (DCs), activating them to express costimulatory molecules and secrete IL-1β and IL-12p40. In vivo, Nano-11 enhances antigen-specific antibody responses comparably to aluminum adjuvants, even at lower doses. It induces a transient, localized inflammatory response primarily involving monocytes/macrophages, clears gradually over three weeks without systemic distribution, and effectively targets antigens to migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes. Its plant-based origin makes it a potentially cost-effective and safe adjuvant candidate.

